/-!
# GST CLASSICAL HODGE — PROJECTIVE SPAN -> WORD -> DIRECT ORBIT SATURATION

This layer removes another artificial interface from the geometry-first Hodge
route.

The repository already contains two native geometric languages at one weight:

* the rational projective-correspondence span generated by actual scheme
  endomorphisms of the smooth projective carrier;
* the free finite projective-word algebra generated by the same actual scheme
  endomorphisms, with rational scaling and addition available as constructors.

These are not independent geometric assumptions.  Every element of the
projective-correspondence span is, by the very meaning of span, a finite
rational linear combination of genuine geometric generators.  Hence it can be
compiled into one explicit finite `ProjectiveOperatorWord` with exactly the
same native action.

This compilation lets us formulate a strictly more native Hodge input.  For a
synchronized live source `S` and target Hodge basis sheet `j`, we request only:

* one operator already known to lie in the genuine projective-correspondence
  span;
* one native cycle-class equation saying that this operator sends the live
  source cycle to the correct scalar multiple of the target basis sheet.

No ambient cohomological operator is supplied.  No matrix-unit action on the
whole Hodge fiber is supplied.  No projective word syntax is supplied.  The
word is compiled from span membership, and its cohomological action is then
manufactured automatically from kernel stability and the geometric
cycle-class spine.

Once this source equation is available for every target direction, the direct
orbit saturation layer absorbs the compiled words into the graded geometric
program algebra, so every rational Hodge class lies in the genuine algebraic
orbit.
-/

set_option maxHeartbeats 90000000
set_option maxRecDepth 1000000

noncomputable section

